opendisplay-x11 (0.3.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the iPad's cursor standing still while dragging (for example
    selecting text) or while a menu is open. Pointer movement is now
    received even while another application holds the pointer (XInput 2.2).

 -- Vibhanshu Biswas <16113990+cray2015@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0530

opendisplay-x11 (0.3.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix freezes on the iPad (for example moving over a right-click menu):
    send frames for 150 ms after each change again. With 50 ms the iPad's
    decoder kept the newest picture back until the next change. The settle
    frame from 0.3.4 stays as an extra safety net.

 -- Vibhanshu Biswas <16113990+cray2015@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0530

opendisplay-x11 (0.3.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fewer frames per change: 50 ms after each change plus one settle frame
    once the screen is quiet (catches fades). A window changing 5 times a
    second now costs ~14 % of one core instead of ~35 %; continuous change
    (video) is unchanged.

 -- Vibhanshu Biswas <16113990+cray2015@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:30:00 +0530

opendisplay-x11 (0.3.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A minimized window on the iPad's monitor no longer keeps the stream
    awake (compositors keep minimized windows drawing for previews).
  * Measured performance documented in the README (tools/perf_bench.py).

 -- Vibhanshu Biswas <16113990+cray2015@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0530

opendisplay-x11 (0.3.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Frames are converted and encoded only for a moment after something on
    the iPad's monitor changes, not continuously: a window that updates a
    few times a second (a clock, a system monitor) now costs ~10 % of one
    core instead of ~40 %.

 -- Vibhanshu Biswas <16113990+cray2015@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:30:00 +0530

opendisplay-x11 (0.3.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Performance presets in the settings window: Power saver, Balanced
    (default), Best quality, Custom. A preset sets frame rate, sharpness and
    idle pausing and greys them out; Custom unlocks them.
  * Each iPad's decode limits are honoured automatically (maximum size,
    frame rate and pixel rate from its hello).

 -- Vibhanshu Biswas <16113990+cray2015@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0530

opendisplay-x11 (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Faster: 60 frames per second by default (capped at the iPad's maximum).
  * The cursor is sent separately and drawn by the iPad, so it moves at input
    speed (up to 120 updates a second) instead of with the video; shape
    changes are sent as images. Moving the mouse no longer wakes the paused
    stream.

